To create a program that mimics the deletion of insignificant system files without actually removing any crucial data, you can write a script that simulates the deletion process by printing a message to the console instead of deleting the files. Here's an example using PowerShell:

```powershell
function Delete-FileSimulator {
    [CmdletBinding()]
    param (
        [Parameter(Mandatory=$true)]
        [string]$Path
    )

    Write-Host "Simulating deletion of file: $Path"
}
